      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z &=-3 \\\\ -4x-2y+4z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 4 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 4 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is inconsistent.",
